WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Hi everybody, I'm Jonathan Schrantz and today I

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.720
got another Tactical Challenge for you

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.490
So when you see the image on your screen

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.290
go ahead pause your video and see if you

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.300
can solve it

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.070
So in this position it is White to move

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.330
I will go ahead and give you guys a hint today

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.460
If you haven't already figured it out

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.859
I'm trying to take advantage of the

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:22.020
fact that the Queen doesn't have a whole

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.699
lot of squares that she can go to

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:25.260
She is a little bit close in our territory

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.400
so see if you can somehow take

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.480
advantage of that fact

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.800
Here comes the answer: the best move in this position is

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.630
Re5! -- interfering with the Queen's

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.329
path and making a threat

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:40.829
I won't tell you what it is right away

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:42.660
but let's just look at what happens if we

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.399
play the most direct move we just take

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:46.469
your rook. Hopefully you can see what White

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:49.230
should play in this position: the move that

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.739
traps the Queen is g3 and the Queen

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:54.930
doesn't have anywhere to go so the best

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.030
you can do is at least get another

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.080
piece for it and here White has won some material

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.699
Going back if you see that

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:04.559
you're about to get trapped you may

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:06.299
think you're clever and perhaps you want

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.299
to try and move like h5 not tempted by

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.159
the exchange and i just created square

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:14.070
so my Queen can retreat back to h6 well

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.280
now still g3 is a strong move because after

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.890
you go back to h6 we can grab the pawn

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.259
on a5 -- now the Knight is hanging and

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:24.990
when you retreat the Knight among other

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.689
moves we can take on f5 and then take on

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:30.150
b7 and we have two pawns for the

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.340
exchange and a completely dominant

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.299
position

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:35.909
another very crafty move that you might

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.439
try going back to this position after

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:42.479
Re5 is the move Bd3

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.820
This also might be a confusing way to try to

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.560
confuse your opponent but it should also

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.229
be insufficient after a move like g3

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:52.619
let's try this crafty move: Bc2!

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:55.770
Well White here again get the

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.740
great position after first taking on c2

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.270
then trading the Queens

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.340
and here again White has won some

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.399
material and has a better position

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:08.920
Thank you everybody for watching

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.599
congrats to everybody was able to get

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:11.530
this one right

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.420
As always hit like, share, subscribe and

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.470
we'll see you next week for another

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:20.400
Tactical Challenge!

